    description: "A very keen sense of taste and smell reads the salinity and toxicity of water and is sharpest for metal, oil and other traces of technology, which can be tracked to their source at 68% +2% per level of experience (-20% for any other scent)."
  - name: "Feelers"
    description: "Two prehensile feelers three feet (0.9 m) long work like extra hands for judging shape and identity by touch, and sense light, water temperature, currents and their direction, scent and motion. The penalty for being blind or working in total darkness is only -3."
  - name: "Limited Bio-Regeneration"
    description: "Regrows lost feelers and mustache tendrils in 1D4+1 days, an eye or eye stalk in 1D4+1 weeks, a hand in 1D4+2 weeks and a leg in 1D6+4 weeks. Otherwise heals at twice the human rate."
  - name: "Prehensile Neck and Eye Stalks"
    description: "The neck is two feet (0.6 m) long, stretches a further 5 feet (1.5 m), and bends to see over, under, around and behind the shell; the head turns a full 360 degrees. Each eye stalk stretches 2 feet (0.6 m), turns 360 degrees and can be aimed independently of the other, which is why the race is hard to surprise or attack from behind (see the conditional Perception bonus)."
  - name: "M.D.C. by Location"
    description: "Head and neck 40 (tripled when a helmet and armored neck protection are worn); hands (2) 30 each; arms (2) 55 each; legs (4) 115 each; main body without the shell is P.E. x2 +1D6 per level of experience (the stored M.D.C. pool); shell housing 4D6x10+35 to start as the stat block prints it, though the ability text on printed 44 says 5D6x10+35."
special_abilities:
  - name: "Amphibious Being"
    description: "Breathes both water and air and can stay on dry land for up to four days without submerging (one third of that in a desert). Past four days out of water, every additional 12 hours halves all physical attributes, attacks/actions per melee round and M.D.C., and the Junk Crab dies of dehydration in 1D4 days."
  - name: "Intuitive Mechanical Aptitude"
    description: "A machine savant with an instinct for building and repair. It is expressed through the R.C.C. skills, the spells and the psionic powers the race is given; the entry prints no further figure for it."
  - name: "Conditional bonuses"
    description: "Not added by the sheet: Perception is +6 rather than +4 to detect a surprise attack or an attack from behind, to find salvage, and when working with scrap and machines. Attacks per melee are three, or six when technology is being used. Out of the armored shell (a rarity) the Junk Crab is +3 to dodge, has Prowl at 64% and doubles its Spd."
  - name: "Armored Techno-Shell (Junk Shell)"
    description: "A hand-built housing of M.D.C. scrap carried on the back, not part of the body: the Junk Crab can climb out of it, though it rarely does. Starting M.D.C. is printed two ways, 5D6x10+35 in the ability text (printed 44) and 4D6x10+35 in the stat block (printed 46). The Junk Crab can pull itself wholly inside and close the opening with a sliding door or a sheet of M.D.C. plate, at which point it passes for a heap of debris and cannot be told from wreckage in a ship graveyard, shipwreck or battlefield until it moves; a feeler or eye stalk can be poked out unnoticed to look around. Size is also printed two ways: 10-15 feet (3 to 4.6 m) tall in the introduction, and up to 8 feet (2.4 m) tall and 6 feet (1.8 m) wide and long under Size. Typical shell weight 1,000-2,500 lbs (450 to 1,125 kg). Shell damage is repaired by the Junk Crab in 1D4 hours given suitable material to weld on; shell M.D.C. can be restored but never raised above its total except through the Extra M.D.C. Armor feature. Some shells mount turbo jets good for 30-40 mph (48-64 km or 26 to 34 knots an hour); see the propulsion features."
  - name: "Building the Techno-Shell"
    description: "At level one pick 1D4+1 weapon features (any) and 1D4+4 other features from the Shell Feature entries below. Each new level of experience from level 2 adds one more feature of either kind. Selections may be left unspent and banked, to add items or armor later or to afford a feature that costs two or three selections. A feature may be taken more than once unless its entry says otherwise. These picks are tracked by hand."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Concealed Cargo Container"
    description: "Either one large container the size of a steamer trunk (4x3x3 feet / 1.2 x 0.9 x 0.9 m) or three small ones the size of a tackle box. All lock and seal watertight."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Concealed Handheld Gun/Energy Assault Weapon"
    description: "Weapon feature. A found energy pistol or rifle, waterproofed and adapted to work underwater and on land. It may be a Biomancy or Techno-Wizard weapon, or a wand, scepter or staff with a ranged attack, but a Junk Crab cannot modify a magic item. Purpose: combat and defense. On dry land range, damage and payload are the weapon''s normal figures; underwater range is one third and Mega-Damage is half. Each blast is one melee attack. Rail guns and most projectile weapons are seldom used, being bulky, needing a large heavy ammo drum and losing much of their value underwater; one follows the same rules (normal range and damage on land, one third range and half damage underwater, normal payload) with each burst one melee attack."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Concealed Melee Weapon"
    description: "Weapon feature. A handheld close-combat weapon kept in a hidden housing, with at most its handle visible on close inspection. Any M.D. or S.D.C. weapon; favorites are clubs and bludgeons, war clubs, hammers, Neural Maces, axes, knives and swords, and they prize Vibro-Blades, Techno-Wizard blades and magic weapons."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Concealed Extendable & Retractable Laser Weapon"
    description: "Weapon feature. A light gun that slides or pops out of a shell housing, traversing 180 degrees with a 45 degree arc up and down. Purpose: defense. Range 1,000 feet (305 m) underwater, 2,000 feet (610 m) on dry land or firing from the water''s surface into the air. Damage 2D6 M.D. Each blast is one melee attack. Payload 120 shots, fed by a series of E-Clips or a small generator; a generator recharges 30 blasts per hour."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Concealed Extendable & Retractable Ion Weapon"
    description: "Weapon feature. A light gun that slides or pops out of a shell housing, traversing 180 degrees with a 45 degree arc up and down. Purpose: defense. Range 500 feet (152 m) underwater, 1,000 feet (305 m) on dry land or firing from the water''s surface into the air. Damage 4D6 M.D. Each blast is one melee attack. Payload 60 shots, fed by a series of E-Clips or a small generator; a generator recharges 15 blasts per hour."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Concealed Extendable & Retractable Power Tools"
    description: "Any bionic-style power tool (drill, jackhammer, saw, laser torch and the like), mounted on an arm that extends and retracts or carried as a hand tool. Range: handheld, or 10 feet (3 m) on an extendable arm. Damage as per the tool."
  - name: "Shell Feature: E-Clip Charger"
    description: "Counts as two selections. An E-Clip charger with a portable generator of 1D4 years'' life built into the shell. A better power source, such as a nuclear one with a 15 year life, is a separate purchase."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Electrified Shell"
    description: "May be selected only once. Electrified nodules on the outside of the shell, switched on only after the Junk Crab has withdrawn completely inside. Range: touch. Damage: 3D6 M.D. each time someone tries to touch the shell, and 1D4 M.D. per melee round to anyone within four feet (1.2 m) of it. Fish and most aquatic animals feel the tingle from 100 yards/meters and keep clear. Payload: 12 periods of electrification, each lasting 1D4+1 minutes."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Extra M.D.C. Armor for the Shell"
    description: "Each selection adds 2D4x10+20 M.D.C. to the shell and increases its size and weight by 10%. No more than five selections."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Fixed Position Laser Weapon"
    description: "Weapon feature. A light laser that looks like a pipe or rifle barrel jutting from the shell and fires only where it points, so re-aiming means turning the whole body. Because the neck and eye stalks see all round, one can be mounted on the front, back, sides, top or underbelly; each location is one selection. Purpose: defense. Range 1,000 feet (305 m) underwater, 2,000 feet (610 m) on dry land or firing from the water''s surface into the air. Damage 2D6 M.D. Each blast is one melee attack. Payload 120 shots, fed by a series of E-Clips or a small generator; a generator recharges 30 blasts per hour."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Fixed Position Ion Weapon"
    description: "Weapon feature. As the Fixed Position Laser Weapon apart from its combat figures. Purpose: defense. Range 500 feet (152 m) underwater, 1,000 feet on dry land or firing from the water''s surface into the air (the book prints the metric as 610 m, which does not match 1,000 feet). Damage 3D6 M.D. Each blast is one melee attack. Payload 80 shots, fed by a series of E-Clips or a small generator; a generator recharges 20 blasts per hour."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Hover and Flight Capabilities"
    description: "Counts as two selections. Lets the Junk Crab hover and fly; needs an E-Clip, battery or generator. Speed: hover and VTOL, 60 mph (96 km) maximum. Maximum height 3,000 feet (914 m). +1 to dodge while flying. A standard E-Clip gives 48 hours of flight before recharging, a long E-Clip 60 hours, and a nuclear battery unlimited flight."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Mini-Missile or Torpedo Launcher"
    description: "Weapon feature. A small two-shot launcher that can be built in almost anywhere on the shell. Range one mile (1.6 km). Damage by the type of torpedo or mini-missile. Fires one or both at a time, as one melee attack. Payload two, with reloads carried on the back or belly or in a concealed storage container."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Nuclear Power Supply"
    description: "Counts as three selections and may be selected only once. The kind of supply used in power armor, with an average life of 15 years. Concealed and fixed energy weapon systems built into the shell are wired to it and have an unlimited payload."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Radio, Long-Range and Directional"
    description: "Range 700 miles (1,120 km) underwater and 500 miles (800 km) on dry land or on the water''s surface, with multiple communication frequencies."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Seating for Passengers"
    description: "Two or three seats on the outside of the shell for riders, each with a seatbelt and shoulder harness."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Sensor Pod"
    description: "A pod usually set on the top or sides of the shell, run by Telemechanics or from a remote control and display console that pulls out of the chest or underbelly of the shell. It typically holds a combat and targeting computer linked to every weapon system built into the shell, sonar and radar of the kind fitted to aquatic power armor, and a radiation detector, compass, gyroscope, depth gauge and temperature gauge. Bonuses: +1 to strike with weapons built into the shell and +2 to dodge. Extra pods are backups only and add no further bonus."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Underwater Hover Jet System"
    description: "May be added only once. Lets the Junk Crab move slowly through water and hold position against a current without swimming; needs an E-Clip, battery or generator. Speed 12 mph (19.2 km or 10.4 knots) maximum. A standard E-Clip gives 120 hours of propulsion before recharging, a long E-Clip 164 hours, and a nuclear battery unlimited use."
  - name: "Shell Feature: Underwater Turbo-Jet System"
    description: "Counts as two selections and may be added only once. Drives the Junk Crab through the water like a torpedo or over the surface like a speedboat; needs an E-Clip, battery or generator. Speed 50 mph (80 km or 43 knots) maximum. A standard E-Clip gives 50 hours of propulsion before recharging, a long E-Clip 66 hours, and a nuclear battery unlimited use."
